* the use remains conceptual;
* attribution is preserved;
* the service is not represented as CNIG itself;
* no operational authority is attributed to CNIG;
* no unauthorized operational derivative is created.

---

## 12. No Authority Transfer

CNIG has no operational authority in any system in which it is referenced.

A positive CNIG analysis does not:

* authorize action;
* approve deployment;
* certify safety;
* establish compliance;
* accept risk;
* grant permission;
* guarantee Admissibility.

A negative, provisional, conflicting, or unresolved CNIG analysis does not itself:

* prohibit action;
* block deployment;
* revoke authority;
* reject a transition;
* impose a control.

Any operational consequence belongs to an external authority and governance process.

That external authority must remain separately identified and accountable.

---

